  dialogueColor: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0}
  startingNode:
    dialogueText: 'Humph... So Natalia sent you, huh?

      Well, I''m sorry to
      tell you that if you''re hungry, you''ll have to wait for dinner just like
      every other guest.

      So please, let me do my work.'
    characterEmotion: 1
    characterReaction: 1
    doesItProveAnything: 4
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 6774952466358992965
    isRootNode: 1
    editorPosition: {x: 12, y: 192}
    altDialoguePaths:
    - rid: 3046478981849153621
    guid:
      Part1: 4033970027
      Part2: 1312935628
      Part3: 1634102948
      Part4: 173125467
    tag: 
  allNodes:
  - dialogueText: 'Humph... So Natalia sent you, huh?

      Well, I''m sorry to
      tell you that if you''re hungry, you''ll have to wait for dinner just like
      every other guest.

      So please, let me do my work.'
    characterEmotion: 1
    characterReaction: 1
    doesItProveAnything: 4
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 6774952466358992965
    isRootNode: 1
    editorPosition: {x: 12, y: 192}
    altDialoguePaths:
    - rid: 3046478981849153621
    guid:
      Part1: 4033970027
      Part2: 1312935628
      Part3: 1634102948
      Part4: 173125467
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: "Yes, I know, she sent you in to lie about how \"good\" my cooking
      was so that I would \"feel better\", smile a bit more and not scare the guests
      away when they see me.\nEvery time, she sends some poor guest to do that, and
      every time, they go back sadder than they were when they arrived... and yet
      she never gets the message. \nA word of advice, son: it's best if you don't
      even waste your time trying."
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 767062219271962632
    - rid: 767062219271962633
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 1138.1602, y: 159}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 3005462273
      Part2: 1186196420
      Part3: 3619405476
      Part4: 2018895431
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: '...And you lied to her so that you could come in and talk to me.

      Humph...
      That''s dangerous, but admirable. Definitely more interesting than the alternative.

      Ask
      then, please. It''s not like I''m ever busy in this desolated hotel.'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 767062219271962639
    - rid: 3046478974422614016
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 2609, y: -87.50003}
    altDialoguePaths:
    - rid: 3046478981849153649
    guid:
      Part1: 1052829987
      Part2: 1289779477
      Part3: 388250795
      Part4: 1008944790
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'If you mean "do I know the latest gossip about them", then you''re
      talking to the wrong person.

      I''m terrible with names, faces, and people
      in general. Apparently, according to Natasha, a couple of them are famous;
      not that I could (or cared to) confirm that, of course.

      Now, if what
      you mean is "do you know who I should suspect from"...'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 767062219271962641
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 3709, y: -185}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 3737222326
      Part2: 1121306442
      Part3: 2996202407
      Part4: 396023909
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: "In that case, you couldn't have found a better man for that. \nIf
      there's something I'm good at, is telling who's about to betray you. My betrayal
      radar never fails.\nOtherwise, you would be speaking to a <b>corpse</b> right
      now. Hah!"
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 767062219271962643
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 5217, y: -235}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 594107815
      Part2: 1257147919
      Part3: 559302833
      Part4: 3749320976
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'For once in my life, not EVERYONE in the hotel... which is probably
      a bad sign.

      Some of them are really going out of their way to look suspicious:
      taking pictures in the open, going into loud rants about how "real" their story
      is... coming in here to ask questions.

      But the danger lies on the ones
      that don''t: the ones who don''t leave their place, as if they are waiting
      for something to unfold...'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 3046478974422614018
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 6398.5, y: -271}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 3590403978
      Part2: 1186015036
      Part3: 4019111299
      Part4: 3889511675
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'There''s two men I haven''t seen since right after they checked
      in... who know what they might be doing upstairs.

      At the same time,
      there''s one man who went upstairs for just a minute, came back down and hasn''t
      left the dining hall since then.

      It seems like a weird thing, renting
      a room and not using it. As if he was avoiding whatever''s going on up there...
      or simply kept away by the ones upstairs...'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 3046478974422614020
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 7828, y: -271}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 1745687723
      Part2: 1246678443
      Part3: 2032475547
      Part4: 711998021
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'Isn''t it obvious? You''re more likely to find a snowman than
      a real man in a hundred mile radius.

      How this place even came to be
      is a mystery not even Natalia can answer... and the fact people would stay
      here should be suspicious by itself.

      You must be a real good investigator,
      if you were even capable of finding this place.'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 3046478974422614022
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 3702, y: 71}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 3633809412
      Part2: 1202094892
      Part3: 1917293957
      Part4: 309081675
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'Humph... Well, then it''s best if you don''t... you''d be lucky
      enough to never have to try it.

      I understand why she would pick a war
      veteran for her staff, but she must really hate her guests if she decided to
      put me anywhere near a kitchen.'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 767062219271962635
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 2636.6821, y: 380.02692}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 3644508348
      Part2: 1196827177
      Part3: 70828988
      Part4: 2055379135
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'Not so much "in" the war, more like "half a mile away" from it.

      I
      was trained to swiftly get one bullet in people''s brains, so that lesser soldiers
      wouldn''t have to waste three hundred bullets just to injure a leg.

      Not
      that that fact spared me from the horrors of war... if anything, it made me
      stare at them through a 25x telescopic lens.'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 767062219271962637
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 3965.6824, y: 396.02695}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 3036664030
      Part2: 1257445403
      Part3: 1589302673
      Part4: 1385208169
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: "They sure wish that was the case... but no, I was discharged because
      I was too good for my own sake.\nNot at shooting targets, necessarily... but
      at telling which the <b>real</b> targets were. \nI always know when someone
      is willing to betray their comrades, and that made me real dangerous for them
      to keep me."
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 3046478974422614024
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 5285.39, y: 515}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 1435620620
      Part2: 1327145785
      Part3: 3224192156
      Part4: 833541254
    tag: 
  - dialogueText: 'I never did, but, you see, in a place as miserable as this, working
      is less about being good at your job, and more about being able to <b>survive</b>
      it.

      Anyone would run away from a place like this... but to me, this
      is nowhere near the worst thing I had to endure.

      Long story short: I''m
      sorry if the food sucks, but literally no-one else would ever take my place.'
    characterEmotion: 0
    characterReaction: 0
    doesItProveAnything: 0
    isKey: 0
    responses:
    - rid: 3046478974422614026
    isRootNode: 0
    editorPosition: {x: 6648.3906, y: 473.99997}
    altDialoguePaths: []
    guid:
      Part1: 1308538176
      Part2: 1294683680
      Part3: 1642293137
      Part4: 642065146
    tag: 
